.TH MLH-GNOME-TERMINAL 1 "2026-10-29" "mlh 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mlh-gnome-terminal \- launch GNOME Terminal with the GTK IBus module
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mlh-gnome-terminal
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Starts a separate GNOME Terminal process with GTK_IM_MODULE=ibus, or opens
a window in the existing separate process. This can help applications without
surrounding-text support on GNOME Wayland. Options are passed to gnome-terminal.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mlh-ibus (1),
.BR gnome-terminal (1)
